[Screams]

782
00:36:12,638 --> 00:36:15,542
Damn bumpus’s dinosaurs.

783
00:36:20,412 --> 00:36:22,382
Save the meat loaf.

784
00:36:26,652 --> 00:36:28,653
Yeah, this happens
a couple times a day.

785
00:36:34,260 --> 00:36:36,295
No! They’re my friends!

786
00:36:36,295 --> 00:36:39,098
Run. Must run.

787
00:36:39,098 --> 00:36:40,398
Amway.

788
00:36:45,503 --> 00:36:46,705
Whaa.

789
00:36:48,173 --> 00:36:50,542
Hey, it’s a full aspirin
out tonight.

790
00:36:52,245 --> 00:36:54,813
Ugh. Glad the dinosaur
got the kid.

791
00:36:54,813 --> 00:36:57,082
Really distracted him.

792
00:36:59,052 --> 00:37:00,285
God.

793
00:37:00,285 --> 00:37:01,287
Thank you.

794
00:37:01,287 --> 00:37:02,688
[Grunts]

795
00:37:02,688 --> 00:37:04,790
I think we’ve
outrun them.

796
00:37:04,790 --> 00:37:07,760
You are a penguin?

797
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:09,795
No, i’m a puffin.

798
00:37:09,795 --> 00:37:12,598
No. I’m a sister.

799
00:37:12,598 --> 00:37:13,598
Not a penguin.

800
00:37:13,598 --> 00:37:16,435
You know,
one of the sledge girls.

801
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:19,738
You know...

802
00:37:19,738 --> 00:37:22,775
How is it you know
english today

803
00:37:22,775 --> 00:37:23,875
when you didn’t
know english yesterday?

804
00:37:23,875 --> 00:37:25,645
Uh, bad screenwriting,
really.

805
00:37:25,645 --> 00:37:27,980
It was hard for me
to understand him.

806
00:37:27,980 --> 00:37:29,415
For all the problems
I had,

807
00:37:29,415 --> 00:37:32,217
maybe I just didn’t want
to be a part of his.

808
00:37:32,217 --> 00:37:34,653
He explained to me how
quickly he could learn,

809
00:37:34,653 --> 00:37:37,990
how his vocal cords needed
to adjust to speak our tongue,

810
00:37:37,990 --> 00:37:39,658
and how he had heard
our words before.

811
00:37:39,658 --> 00:37:40,660
Go ahead.

812
00:37:40,660 --> 00:37:42,093
His eyes were so honest,

813
00:37:42,093 --> 00:37:45,632
but still there was a part
of him that I didn’t trust.

814
00:37:45,632 --> 00:37:46,632
And who are you?

815
00:37:46,632 --> 00:37:47,667
A tool.

816
00:37:47,667 --> 00:37:49,802
I’m a boxwrench.

817
00:37:49,802 --> 00:37:51,137
And you come from--?

818
00:37:51,137 --> 00:37:52,905
Uh, just let me check the wind
and i’ll tell ya.

819
00:37:52,905 --> 00:37:54,540
Never mind.

820
00:37:54,540 --> 00:37:56,275
[Bells clanging]

821
00:37:56,275 --> 00:37:58,243
Trains bringing in food
for the roommates.

822
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:06,252
Well, I suppose one of us
has to play harmonica.

823
00:38:07,887 --> 00:38:10,890
Want a little
convent-issued pot here?

824
00:38:10,890 --> 00:38:12,257
Here.

825
00:38:14,627 --> 00:38:18,130
Will you chew it
and regurgitate it for me?

826
00:38:18,130 --> 00:38:19,465
Mm.

827
00:38:19,465 --> 00:38:21,467
[Laughs]

828
00:38:21,467 --> 00:38:24,537
Whoa.
I needed that jerky.

829
00:38:26,272 --> 00:38:27,305
You’re human.

830
00:38:27,305 --> 00:38:28,507
And you’re
putting up with me.

831
00:38:28,507 --> 00:38:30,408
I am...Tool.

832
00:38:30,408 --> 00:38:31,743
Call me "snap-on."

833
00:38:31,743 --> 00:38:35,080
And you’re from up there.

834
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:36,682
The pagam.

835
00:38:36,682 --> 00:38:40,687
The first were harvested
from this world,

836
00:38:40,687 --> 00:38:43,422
like, trackers long ago.

837
00:38:43,422 --> 00:38:44,657
I preferred his grunting.

838
00:38:44,657 --> 00:38:47,393
We are used to build

839
00:38:47,393 --> 00:38:49,662
because...

840
00:38:49,662 --> 00:38:51,363
We have these.

841
00:38:51,363 --> 00:38:53,465
Hamburglar finger puppets.

842
00:38:54,533 --> 00:38:56,202
The master

843
00:38:56,202 --> 00:38:59,438
do not have these.

844
00:38:59,438 --> 00:39:00,973
They can make
their own thumbs,

845
00:39:00,973 --> 00:39:03,042
but they just
don’t want to?

846
00:39:03,042 --> 00:39:06,245
They want
us to do the work.

847
00:39:06,245 --> 00:39:09,682
Yeah, I knew
a few pimps in my time.

848
00:39:09,682 --> 00:39:10,817
Pimps?

849
00:39:10,817 --> 00:39:12,250
Did you know rooster?

850
00:39:12,250 --> 00:39:14,353
You wouldn’t understand.

851
00:39:14,353 --> 00:39:16,622
Like the bible says,

852
00:39:16,622 --> 00:39:18,390
my thoughts
are not your thoughts.

853
00:39:18,390 --> 00:39:21,793
Neither are your ways
my ways,

854
00:39:21,793 --> 00:39:22,995
says the lord.

855
00:39:22,995 --> 00:39:24,630
Jack lord.

856
00:39:25,898 --> 00:39:27,667
This is a con.

857
00:39:27,667 --> 00:39:29,168
No, no, no, no.

858
00:39:29,168 --> 00:39:31,570
No. No trick. No lie.

859
00:39:31,570 --> 00:39:34,173
How does an alien-bred human

860
00:39:34,173 --> 00:39:36,775
know quotes from the bible?

861
00:39:36,775 --> 00:39:39,778
In the world where
I am from,

862
00:39:39,778 --> 00:39:43,382
in the place where
the tools are kept

863
00:39:43,382 --> 00:39:46,618
are...
Unsketched with words.

864
00:39:46,618 --> 00:39:49,588
A phrase
told in darkness.

865
00:39:49,588 --> 00:39:52,725
I have heard
your language before.

866
00:39:52,725 --> 00:39:56,562
Well, um, explain this
so I can understand it.

867
00:39:56,562 --> 00:39:58,463
Why are we on this train?

868
00:39:58,463 --> 00:40:00,265
This place

869
00:40:00,265 --> 00:40:02,902
was the most
important story.

870
00:40:02,902 --> 00:40:05,503
Our dream.

871
00:40:05,503 --> 00:40:07,440
Our heaven.

872
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:08,473
And now,

873
00:40:08,473 --> 00:40:09,508
our gang.

874
00:40:09,508 --> 00:40:10,810
I’m free.

875
00:40:10,810 --> 00:40:13,912
- [Voice over]
He was so honest.
- What?

876
00:40:13,912 --> 00:40:15,982
I explained to him,
about the heavens.

877
00:40:15,982 --> 00:40:18,050
I was studying
to become a nun.

878
00:40:18,050 --> 00:40:19,152
Mm-hmm.

879
00:40:19,152 --> 00:40:20,218
But now i’m having
second thoughts.

880
00:40:20,218 --> 00:40:22,822
I’m mary.
This is my story.

881
00:40:22,822 --> 00:40:25,023
When I was younger,
I ran away and

882
00:40:25,023 --> 00:40:27,527
I have a past that
i’m not proud of.

883
00:40:27,527 --> 00:40:29,027
That’s why I kept
a scrapbook.

884
00:40:29,027 --> 00:40:30,028
[Laughs]

885
00:40:30,028 --> 00:40:31,530
I found the church

886
00:40:31,530 --> 00:40:32,698
and they helped me.

887
00:40:34,267 --> 00:40:37,102
But just recently
a friend of mine, um,

888
00:40:37,102 --> 00:40:38,537
died of a drug overdose.

889
00:40:38,537 --> 00:40:39,672
Pepcid ac.

890
00:40:39,672 --> 00:40:42,675
I blame myself
for her death.

891
00:40:42,675 --> 00:40:44,143
I don’t know.

892
00:40:44,143 --> 00:40:46,945
I feel somehow responsible.

893
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:50,248
I guess that’s why I blame
myself for the death.

894
00:40:51,317 --> 00:40:53,452
Yeah, I made her swallow
a pound of coke.

895
00:40:53,452 --> 00:40:54,820
She was yelling,
"please stop,"

896
00:40:54,820 --> 00:40:56,588
but still.

897
00:40:56,588 --> 00:40:58,490
[Bells ringing]

898
00:40:58,490 --> 00:40:59,792
The only thing
that keeps me going

899
00:40:59,792 --> 00:41:02,027
is my all-bells cd.

900
00:41:09,402 --> 00:41:10,668
Hey, you know what, guys?

901
00:41:10,668 --> 00:41:11,670
What?

902
00:41:11,670 --> 00:41:12,672
We have been remiss.

903
00:41:12,672 --> 00:41:13,672
I know what
you’re thinking.

904
00:41:13,672 --> 00:41:16,008
Yeah,
you know we have never,

905
00:41:16,008 --> 00:41:17,042
like in the movie,

906
00:41:17,042 --> 00:41:18,877
thanked pearl
for not killing us.

907
00:41:18,877 --> 00:41:19,878
Not once.

908
00:41:19,878 --> 00:41:21,213
Well, let’s do it.

909
00:41:21,213 --> 00:41:22,247
Right now.

910
00:41:22,247 --> 00:41:23,682
Yeah.

911
00:41:23,682 --> 00:41:25,050
Hello, pearl?

912
00:41:25,050 --> 00:41:26,652
[Man over intercom]
Satellite killer launch--

913
00:41:26,652 --> 00:41:29,588
six...
Five...

914
00:41:29,588 --> 00:41:32,525
Four...
Three...

915
00:41:32,525 --> 00:41:33,525
Two...

916
00:41:33,525 --> 00:41:34,893
Yeah? What?

917
00:41:34,893 --> 00:41:35,995
Well, uh, pearl,

918
00:41:35,995 --> 00:41:38,463
I don’t know
how else to say this.

919
00:41:38,463 --> 00:41:40,365
Uh, thank you
for not killing us.

920
00:41:40,365 --> 00:41:41,667
- Yeah.
- Right.

921
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:47,438
Huh?

922
00:41:48,507 --> 00:41:50,542
Well, that’s okay.

923
00:41:50,542 --> 00:41:51,710
Ah--

924
00:41:51,710 --> 00:41:55,280
I would never...

925
00:41:55,280 --> 00:41:56,982
Kill...

926
00:41:56,982 --> 00:42:00,452
Brain guy, get over here.

927
00:42:00,452 --> 00:42:03,222
Hello.

928
00:42:03,222 --> 00:42:04,457
Well, you know,

929
00:42:04,457 --> 00:42:06,625
things get pretty tense
between us.

930
00:42:06,625 --> 00:42:08,193
What with one thing
or another, I mean,

931
00:42:08,193 --> 00:42:09,762
you could easily
have killed us.

932
00:42:09,762 --> 00:42:10,762
And you didn’t do that.

933
00:42:10,762 --> 00:42:13,498
So--so thanks.

934
00:42:14,667 --> 00:42:15,968
Really, that’s okay.

935
00:42:15,968 --> 00:42:16,968
Ah--

936
00:42:16,968 --> 00:42:18,337
I guess I just...

937
00:42:18,337 --> 00:42:20,305
Take it for granted
that I would never...

938
00:42:22,373 --> 00:42:23,575
How do you turn
the rocket?

939
00:42:23,575 --> 00:42:25,410
Well, first you say
you want to kill them,

940
00:42:25,410 --> 00:42:26,945
then you say you don’t
want to kill them.

941
00:42:26,945 --> 00:42:28,280
I mean,
what am I supposed to do?

942
00:42:28,280 --> 00:42:30,648
Well, I can’t
kill them now.

943
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:32,483
Really, don’t think
a second thing about it.

944
00:42:32,483 --> 00:42:34,487
"It would be so fun to kill
mike and the bots today."

945
00:42:34,487 --> 00:42:35,587
[Grunts]

946
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:38,023
Um, anything else
you guys wanna add?

947
00:42:38,023 --> 00:42:39,123
I don’t think so.

948
00:42:39,123 --> 00:42:41,393
Just thanks.
For not killing us.

949
00:42:41,393 --> 00:42:42,795
Yeah.

950
00:42:42,795 --> 00:42:44,363
Yeah. That’s okay.

951
00:42:44,363 --> 00:42:45,630
Don’t worry about it.

952
00:42:45,630 --> 00:42:47,132
But, but, but,
aren’t you killing them now?

953
00:42:47,132 --> 00:42:48,400
Shh.

954
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:49,802
They’re thanking you
for not killing them,

955
00:42:49,802 --> 00:42:50,802
but you’re killing them--

956
00:42:50,802 --> 00:42:52,672
ugh. Oh.
[Grunts]

957
00:42:52,672 --> 00:42:55,073
There. Ready.

958
00:42:55,073 --> 00:42:57,810
Well, I guess
that’s about it.

959
00:42:57,810 --> 00:42:58,810
Just thanks for not ki--

960
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:01,880
[shouts]

961
00:43:01,880 --> 00:43:02,915
Hey.

962
00:43:02,915 --> 00:43:04,317
Hey, you tried
to kill us.

963
00:43:04,317 --> 00:43:05,317
What the--?

964
00:43:06,418 --> 00:43:08,187
No!

965
00:43:08,187 --> 00:43:10,455
I didn’t. No.

966
00:43:10,455 --> 00:43:11,457
Never.

967
00:43:11,457 --> 00:43:12,457
Yes, you did.

968
00:43:12,457 --> 00:43:13,458
Ugh.

969
00:43:13,458 --> 00:43:14,793
[Scoffs]

970
00:43:14,793 --> 00:43:16,562
Well,
I just think this changes
everything.

971
00:43:16,562 --> 00:43:19,498
I suppose there’s other times
you’ve tried to kill us too.

972
00:43:19,498 --> 00:43:20,698
Oh,
now we have movie sign.

973
00:43:20,698 --> 00:43:22,702
Can I even trust that?

974
00:43:22,702 --> 00:43:24,637
I don’t know.

975
00:43:34,413 --> 00:43:35,713
Sister ann?

976
00:43:35,713 --> 00:43:36,715
Are you all right?

977
00:43:36,715 --> 00:43:39,352
I can’t believe it.
Wow.

978
00:43:39,352 --> 00:43:41,353
Ever since yesterday
at the burial

979
00:43:41,353 --> 00:43:43,455
i’ve been asking myself...

980
00:43:43,455 --> 00:43:45,023
How much
do undertakers make?

981
00:43:45,023 --> 00:43:46,358
What I missed.

982
00:43:46,358 --> 00:43:48,693
You didn’t miss anything,
my dear.

983
00:43:48,693 --> 00:43:50,862
It wasn’t your fault.

984
00:43:50,862 --> 00:43:52,463
How come I wasn’t taken?

985
00:43:52,463 --> 00:43:53,832
Because you weren’t.

986
00:43:53,832 --> 00:43:54,833
And that’s that.

987
00:43:54,833 --> 00:43:56,602
So shut your trap.

988
00:43:56,602 --> 00:44:01,573
I don’t know
if i’m going to take
my final vows next week.

989
00:44:01,573 --> 00:44:03,542
I have a nail appointment.

990
00:44:03,542 --> 00:44:05,377
Because of terry jo?
That’s what this is--?

991
00:44:05,377 --> 00:44:07,913
You know what I was
before I came here.

992
00:44:07,913 --> 00:44:10,148
Sister william
looks concerned.

993
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:11,917
Well, you had a record.

994
00:44:11,917 --> 00:44:12,952
So did mary magdalene.

995
00:44:12,952 --> 00:44:14,387
I was a whore

996
00:44:14,387 --> 00:44:16,088
doing tricks in back alleys.

997
00:44:16,088 --> 00:44:17,155
I sold drugs.

998
00:44:17,155 --> 00:44:18,623
Sister ann, that was then.

999
00:44:18,623 --> 00:44:20,425
This is then too.
It’s weird.

1000
00:44:20,425 --> 00:44:22,093
I’m very proud of you now.

1001
00:44:22,093 --> 00:44:24,328
You’re bringing in
a lot of cash
to the convent.

1002
00:44:24,328 --> 00:44:26,732
I’m not.

1003
00:44:27,833 --> 00:44:29,435
Well, then.

1004
00:44:29,435 --> 00:44:31,870
We have a problem here,
don’t we?

1005
00:44:31,870 --> 00:44:35,173
She was smart, sister.

1006
00:44:35,173 --> 00:44:37,977
Good. Tough.

1007
00:44:37,977 --> 00:44:40,012
She was built "ford tough."

1008
00:44:40,012 --> 00:44:41,580
Sister.

1009
00:44:41,580 --> 00:44:43,548
I should have been there
for her when she needed me.

1010
00:44:43,548 --> 00:44:45,150
Sister ann.
Why don’t you take
the weekend?

1011
00:44:45,150 --> 00:44:46,652
Go out to the track
or something.

1012
00:44:46,652 --> 00:44:48,887
Visit your friends
and family.

1013
00:44:48,887 --> 00:44:51,457
Perfection is not
one of the requirements.

1014
00:44:51,457 --> 00:44:52,892
Faith is.

1015
00:44:52,892 --> 00:44:55,327
Sister.
Do you believe in signs?

1016
00:44:55,327 --> 00:44:57,528
I believe in
"yield from right."

1017
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,230
I guess I do.

1018
00:44:59,230 --> 00:45:01,267
Really? I--i don’t know
what to say.

1019
00:45:01,267 --> 00:45:02,700
I thought you were gonna
say no.

1020
00:45:02,700 --> 00:45:03,835
Keep your eyes open.

1021
00:45:03,835 --> 00:45:05,203
Can’t trust these nuns.

1022
00:45:05,203 --> 00:45:07,505
God always answers prayers.

1023
00:45:07,505 --> 00:45:09,975
But only from catholics.

1024
00:45:12,343 --> 00:45:15,047
We’ll take a brief break
from my flashback now.

1025
00:45:15,047 --> 00:45:16,982
What about the tracker?

1026
00:45:16,982 --> 00:45:19,485
What happens now?

1027
00:45:19,485 --> 00:45:21,753
The tracker will rest.

1028
00:45:21,753 --> 00:45:23,955
Then go back.

1029
00:45:23,955 --> 00:45:25,957
What was I talking about?

1030
00:45:25,957 --> 00:45:27,893
To where it first found us.

1031
00:45:27,893 --> 00:45:29,260
Is he talking about
a "warwolf?"

1032
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:32,163
I don’t believe this.

1033
00:45:33,432 --> 00:45:37,502
This is a city.
Twelve-million puddy-tats.

1034
00:45:37,502 --> 00:45:39,403
Are you going back?

1035
00:45:39,403 --> 00:45:40,638
Yes.

1036
00:45:40,638 --> 00:45:42,842
But the tracker
has your scent now.

1037
00:45:42,842 --> 00:45:43,842
Tough.

1038
00:45:43,842 --> 00:45:44,877
He’ll have to deal with it.

1039
00:45:44,877 --> 00:45:48,680
If I go with you,
it will find me.

1040
00:45:48,680 --> 00:45:51,082
Well then you better
get back on the train.

1041
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:54,285
Say, by the way,
what is "kiss?"

1042
00:45:54,285 --> 00:45:57,055
I do not understand.

1043
00:45:57,055 --> 00:45:58,457
This is something
I have to do.

1044
00:45:58,457 --> 00:46:02,227
I’d like to give you
some big words of wisdom,

1045
00:46:02,227 --> 00:46:03,762
but I just don’t have any.

1046
00:46:03,762 --> 00:46:05,530
My mind’s blank.

1047
00:46:05,530 --> 00:46:07,332
You do what you have to do.

1048
00:46:07,332 --> 00:46:08,833
Goodbye.

1049
00:46:08,833 --> 00:46:10,768
We don’t have a permit
to shoot on the curb.

1050
00:46:12,872 --> 00:46:15,307
Am I a wild and crazy guy?

1051
00:46:15,307 --> 00:46:17,608
What are you doing?

1052
00:46:17,608 --> 00:46:18,977
Doing what I believe to.

1053
00:46:18,977 --> 00:46:21,078
Is that okay at you?

1054
00:46:21,078 --> 00:46:23,182
And what’s that?

1055
00:46:23,182 --> 00:46:24,783
I’m going with you.

1056
00:46:24,783 --> 00:46:26,618
Look.

1057
00:46:26,618 --> 00:46:28,320
Let’s get this straight.

1058
00:46:28,320 --> 00:46:29,320
I work alone.

1059
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:31,290
I nun outta my home.

1060
00:46:31,290 --> 00:46:33,125
Alone.

1061
00:46:33,125 --> 00:46:36,462
By myself.
I want to be alone.

1062
00:46:36,462 --> 00:46:42,033
Better is a neighbor
that is near
than a brother far off.

1063
00:46:42,033 --> 00:46:44,503
Uh, that’s from one of them
"chicken soup" books.

1064
00:46:44,503 --> 00:46:46,438
I don’t wanna
talk about this.

1065
00:46:48,373 --> 00:46:50,308
Could you button my shirt?

1066
00:46:52,277 --> 00:46:56,915
I’m gonna call sister gary
and see if she can cover
my shift.

1067
00:46:56,915 --> 00:47:00,152
The number you have reached
is not in service.

1068
00:47:00,152 --> 00:47:02,587
Oh, vatican.
Pay your phone bill.

1069
00:47:04,222 --> 00:47:06,057
Heaven’s a mess,
isn’t it?

1070
00:47:06,057 --> 00:47:07,625
I don’t know.
I like it.

1071
00:47:07,625 --> 00:47:11,497
"The alien and the nun."
This fall on cbs.

1072
00:47:11,497 --> 00:47:14,365
How many people
got murdered today? Huh?

1073
00:47:14,365 --> 00:47:18,537
Or raped? Beaten?
Oh. Missing!

1074
00:47:18,537 --> 00:47:19,938
You’re upset.

1075
00:47:19,938 --> 00:47:21,038
Yeah, i’m upset.

1076
00:47:21,038 --> 00:47:22,507
Didn’t my acting
convey that?

1077
00:47:22,507 --> 00:47:24,142
But you want
to help your friends.

1078
00:47:24,142 --> 00:47:26,212
And that’s different.
I know them.

1079
00:47:26,212 --> 00:47:27,712
You don’t know me.

1080
00:47:27,712 --> 00:47:30,282
You helped me.

1081
00:47:30,282 --> 00:47:33,252
Greater love
has no man than this...

1082
00:47:33,252 --> 00:47:36,187
Than a man lay down
his life...

1083
00:47:36,187 --> 00:47:37,222
Heard it.

1084
00:47:37,222 --> 00:47:38,357
For his friend.

1085
00:47:38,357 --> 00:47:41,560
Ugh.
I gotta get outta here.

1086
00:47:41,560 --> 00:47:43,895
Should we be worried
about our friends?

1087
00:47:43,895 --> 00:47:46,465
That is what I want to be.

1088
00:47:46,465 --> 00:47:47,598
What?

1089
00:47:47,598 --> 00:47:49,367
A man.

1090
00:47:49,367 --> 00:47:50,868
You are a man.

1091
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:55,140
No.
I mean, greater love.

1092
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:57,142
That kind of man.

1093
00:47:57,142 --> 00:47:59,343
You better be careful
what you wish for.

1094
00:47:59,343 --> 00:48:01,078
Sister mary despair.

1095
00:48:01,078 --> 00:48:02,180
[Laughs]

1096
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:12,290
Ah, life is good.
I live in maui
and I got a monster mag.

1097
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:14,893
[Laughs]

1098
00:48:14,893 --> 00:48:16,562
[Growls]

1099
00:48:16,562 --> 00:48:19,430
♪ Wastin’ away again
in margaritaville ♪

1100
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:23,368
Ew.

1101
00:48:25,470 --> 00:48:29,240
He has the live,
supple figure
of james doohan.

1102
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:32,945
[Growling]

1103
00:48:34,578 --> 00:48:36,815
A man was snapped at by
a forced-perspective puppet
today.

1104
00:48:36,815 --> 00:48:38,417
We’re going
on the assumption

1105
00:48:38,417 --> 00:48:42,120
that some animal
out of the hills
has gone on a rampage.

1106
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:44,255
The body found here
at third street

1107
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:46,558
makes four deaths
in six hours.

1108
00:48:46,558 --> 00:48:48,560
This creature knows
where it’s going.

1109
00:48:48,560 --> 00:48:51,363
I want cars posted
all along this route.

1110
00:48:51,363 --> 00:48:52,897
Make ’em all tercels.

1111
00:48:52,897 --> 00:48:55,567
Stay in close radio contact
at all times.

1112
00:48:55,567 --> 00:48:56,935
Let’s go.

1113
00:48:59,303 --> 00:49:00,572
Is god out there?

1114
00:49:00,572 --> 00:49:02,307
He is out there, man!

1115
00:49:02,307 --> 00:49:05,310
God of gods.
King of kings.

1116
00:49:05,310 --> 00:49:07,245
You don’t even know
what you’re saying, do you?

1117
00:49:07,245 --> 00:49:08,747
[Gibberish]

1118
00:49:08,747 --> 00:49:09,748
You don’t.

1119
00:49:09,748 --> 00:49:11,583
[Gibberish]

1120
00:49:11,583 --> 00:49:14,653
What’s out there?
Is heaven out there?

1121
00:49:14,653 --> 00:49:15,987
Earth is heaven.

1122
00:49:15,987 --> 00:49:18,223
Thanks to olestra.

1123
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:21,493
And the supreme being
is what?

1124
00:49:21,493 --> 00:49:22,860
Well,
it’s not earl holliman.

1125
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:25,430
Handlers. Masters.

1126
00:49:25,430 --> 00:49:28,467
No, no, no, no. Not them.
Greater than them.

1127
00:49:28,467 --> 00:49:31,235
What is your word
for "boring?"

1128
00:49:31,235 --> 00:49:32,937
[Laughs]

1129
00:49:32,937 --> 00:49:35,840
The movie’s dragging,
then they show us soccer.

1130
00:49:35,840 --> 00:49:37,375
Good.

1131
00:49:37,375 --> 00:49:40,078
Soccer’s my game.
I’ve no arms, ya see.

1132
00:49:40,078 --> 00:49:42,313
Aah!

1133
00:49:42,313 --> 00:49:43,315
[Phone ringing]

1134
00:49:43,315 --> 00:49:44,348
"Puffy hat police."

1135
00:49:44,348 --> 00:49:45,583
Western division.

1136
00:49:45,583 --> 00:49:46,818
Officer fry speaking.

1137
00:49:46,818 --> 00:49:47,952
How may I help you?

1138
00:49:47,952 --> 00:49:49,187
Hello.

1139
00:49:49,187 --> 00:49:50,422
This is mailboxes etc.

1140
00:49:50,422 --> 00:49:51,723
People really need our boxes.

1141
00:49:51,723 --> 00:49:52,790
Be calm, sir.

1142
00:49:52,790 --> 00:49:54,793
Help us. Please.

1143
00:49:54,793 --> 00:49:55,927
[Laughs]

1144
00:49:55,927 --> 00:49:59,630
Man. Why’d we take
the train to sacramento?

1145
00:50:01,032 --> 00:50:03,068
I’m supposed to get you folks
back in the movie.

1146
00:50:04,770 --> 00:50:08,340
10-4 unit 41-k.
905-v in progress.

1147
00:50:08,340 --> 00:50:10,275
Fifth street warehouse.
Code three.

1148
00:50:10,275 --> 00:50:13,378
It’s the world’s
most put-upon nun.

1149
00:50:15,680 --> 00:50:18,883
This is boris becker
reporting live.

1150
00:50:20,018 --> 00:50:22,287
This is wcng reporter...

1151
00:50:22,287 --> 00:50:23,288
[Laughter]

1152
00:50:23,288 --> 00:50:24,288
Reporting to you live

1153
00:50:24,288 --> 00:50:26,290
from the fifth street
warehouse

1154
00:50:26,290 --> 00:50:30,762
where there has been
a reported animal attack.

1155
00:50:30,762 --> 00:50:32,697
[Laughter]

1156
00:50:32,697 --> 00:50:34,632
Ted nugent helps out.

1157
00:50:36,902 --> 00:50:39,503
More updates as they occur.

1158
00:50:39,503 --> 00:50:41,707
Thanks for playing reporter
and camera guy with me.

1159
00:50:41,707 --> 00:50:44,675
I think the cardboard camera’s
working good.

1160
00:50:44,675 --> 00:50:46,412
[Laughter]

1161
00:50:46,412 --> 00:50:48,413
Captain,
there are employees

1162
00:50:48,413 --> 00:50:50,615
still in the plant
at the back of a store room.

1163
00:50:50,615 --> 00:50:51,817
He’s reporting
over a baby monitor.

1164
00:50:51,817 --> 00:50:54,718
Joey,
lead in the tactical team.

1165
00:50:54,718 --> 00:50:56,888
You take the point.

1166
00:50:58,590 --> 00:51:03,128
Ugh. Now, I have unbridled
enthusiasm for boxes, mike,

1167
00:51:03,128 --> 00:51:04,262
you know that.

1168
00:51:04,262 --> 00:51:06,230
But even I think
they’ve overdone

1169
00:51:06,230 --> 00:51:09,100
