1186
00:51:54,545 --> 00:51:57,282
I just found the blood stains.
This looks fresh.

1187
00:51:57,282 --> 00:51:58,750
And i’ve tried
scrubbing them out.

1188
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:00,885
You sure it’s not ketchup?

1189
00:52:00,885 --> 00:52:05,023
No, sir. It’s real.

1190
00:52:05,023 --> 00:52:07,092
Focus on, uh, polaris.

1191
00:52:07,092 --> 00:52:09,928
And arctic cat.

1192
00:52:09,928 --> 00:52:12,397
What happened?

1193
00:52:12,397 --> 00:52:14,098
You two. Follow me.

1194
00:52:14,098 --> 00:52:16,835
They were transferred
to a costa-gavras film.

1195
00:52:18,403 --> 00:52:21,138
All patrols.
Northeast corner.

1196
00:52:21,138 --> 00:52:23,073
Your lights are on.

1197
00:52:25,277 --> 00:52:28,580
Uh, anybody got
a bloody glove we could plant?

1198
00:52:30,615 --> 00:52:32,583
Sweet jesus.

1199
00:52:34,085 --> 00:52:35,753
Leo.

1200
00:52:35,753 --> 00:52:39,357
Reminds me of the time
chief gates chunked all over
headquarters.

1201
00:52:39,357 --> 00:52:40,358
Ugh.

1202
00:52:40,358 --> 00:52:42,727
Sometimes tools will run.

1203
00:52:42,727 --> 00:52:46,263
When the trackers catch them,
it’s like this.

1204
00:52:47,632 --> 00:52:49,968
So, uh, wally,
you need a doctor or...?

1205
00:52:49,968 --> 00:52:52,470
[Gunshots]

1206
00:52:52,470 --> 00:52:55,473
The dinosaur is skeet shooting
off the port bow.

1207
00:52:59,243 --> 00:53:01,145
[Growling]

1208
00:53:01,145 --> 00:53:02,413
Hey, it’s coming back.

1209
00:53:02,413 --> 00:53:05,383
The movie that
pushes over boxes.

1210
00:53:05,383 --> 00:53:06,985
Don’t shoot.
Floyd’s behind ’em.

1211
00:53:06,985 --> 00:53:08,085
Might hit each other.

1212
00:53:08,085 --> 00:53:09,487
I’ve got floyd.

1213
00:53:09,487 --> 00:53:11,322
Can you kill him with that?

1214
00:53:11,322 --> 00:53:13,292
Yeah. Here. Cut here.

1215
00:53:13,292 --> 00:53:14,392
It’s the softest place.

1216
00:53:14,392 --> 00:53:16,160
Ooh.

1217
00:53:16,160 --> 00:53:17,162
How long?

1218
00:53:17,162 --> 00:53:18,630
Just a moment.

1219
00:53:18,630 --> 00:53:20,598
Don’t miss.

1220
00:53:20,598 --> 00:53:23,902
This is how dinosaurs
see plaid.

1221
00:53:25,603 --> 00:53:27,938
This is a case where parents
should have crushed

1222
00:53:27,938 --> 00:53:29,807
a child’s dream
of becoming a filmmaker.

1223
00:53:29,807 --> 00:53:30,808
Mm. Right.

1224
00:53:30,808 --> 00:53:31,810
Aah!

1225
00:53:31,810 --> 00:53:32,977
So when you edit it,

1226
00:53:32,977 --> 00:53:35,813
it’ll look like I stabbed him,
right?

1227
00:53:39,783 --> 00:53:42,787
I was coming to warn you.
An asteroid...

1228
00:53:42,787 --> 00:53:44,122
Ugh...

1229
00:53:45,890 --> 00:53:49,193
Swat guy who’s dead
must be feelin’ pretty dumb
right now.

1230
00:53:49,193 --> 00:53:51,162
[Beeping]

1231
00:53:51,162 --> 00:53:52,730
That’s mine. I got it.

1232
00:53:52,730 --> 00:53:55,033
Get down!

1233
00:53:55,033 --> 00:53:57,768
Oh. I had a woodchuck
do this to me once.

1234
00:53:57,768 --> 00:53:59,703
[Laughs]

1235
00:54:04,542 --> 00:54:07,478
Well.

1236
00:54:07,478 --> 00:54:09,080
Captain polaris.

1237
00:54:09,080 --> 00:54:10,115
[Laughter]

1238
00:54:10,115 --> 00:54:12,950
Captain polaris?
Are you there?

1239
00:54:12,950 --> 00:54:14,185
Captain polaris?

1240
00:54:14,185 --> 00:54:16,688
We got the bastard, sergeant.

1241
00:54:16,688 --> 00:54:18,623
We’ve got a situation here.

1242
00:54:18,623 --> 00:54:21,258
What do you mean
you got a situation?

1243
00:54:21,258 --> 00:54:24,128
I mean we’ve got more monster
sightings in the city.

1244
00:54:24,128 --> 00:54:26,665
More?
How could there be more?

1245
00:54:26,665 --> 00:54:27,732
They come in packs.

1246
00:54:27,732 --> 00:54:28,733
Or cartons.

1247
00:54:28,733 --> 00:54:30,635
They’re after me.

1248
00:54:30,635 --> 00:54:33,438
They will continue
to hurt people

1249
00:54:33,438 --> 00:54:35,340
until they find me.

1250
00:54:35,340 --> 00:54:36,507
Bring me to them.

1251
00:54:36,507 --> 00:54:38,977
Otis. Smitty.
Place this man under arrest.

1252
00:54:38,977 --> 00:54:40,978
Hey. He just saved you and
everybody in the building

1253
00:54:40,978 --> 00:54:42,013
from that thing.

1254
00:54:42,013 --> 00:54:43,013
That’s right.

1255
00:54:43,013 --> 00:54:44,315
He’s not a criminal.

1256
00:54:44,315 --> 00:54:45,917
He won’t run away
this time.

1257
00:54:45,917 --> 00:54:47,718
Now, if you’ll excuse us,
sister ann,

1258
00:54:47,718 --> 00:54:49,687
your friend’s got
some questions to answer.

1259
00:54:49,687 --> 00:54:51,857
Hey.
How did you know who I was?

1260
00:54:51,857 --> 00:54:54,558
Fred burroughs told us how
he got you to give him a ride,

1261
00:54:54,558 --> 00:54:56,360
but don’t worry.
You’re free to go.

1262
00:54:56,360 --> 00:54:59,597
Fred burroughs.
Somebody look in your rolodex
for a fred burroughs.

1263
00:54:59,597 --> 00:55:02,600
Who’s fred burroughs?

1264
00:55:04,302 --> 00:55:07,472
Fred burroughs! Help me!

1265
00:55:09,573 --> 00:55:13,978
A skinny, belgian idiot
was arraigned on charges
early today.

1266
00:55:15,580 --> 00:55:18,148
Well, I am belgian.

1267
00:55:18,148 --> 00:55:19,583
[Static]

1268
00:55:19,583 --> 00:55:22,720
Hey, the l.a. police
got themselves a boombox.

1269
00:55:22,720 --> 00:55:23,788
And a copier.

1270
00:55:23,788 --> 00:55:24,822
Whoo.

1271
00:55:24,822 --> 00:55:25,857
[Laughs]

1272
00:55:25,857 --> 00:55:26,858
...has caused a number

1273
00:55:26,858 --> 00:55:28,225
of wild animals to escape

1274
00:55:28,225 --> 00:55:29,293
from the zoo.

1275
00:55:29,293 --> 00:55:30,962
They are extremely
dangerous.

1276
00:55:30,962 --> 00:55:34,565
[Imitates monkey]

1277
00:55:36,735 --> 00:55:39,203
Just wait until fred burroughs
gets here, man.

1278
00:55:39,203 --> 00:55:40,838
[Grunts]

1279
00:55:42,007 --> 00:55:43,273
Ugh. Haven’t had hardee’s

1280
00:55:43,273 --> 00:55:44,342
in over an hour.

1281
00:55:44,342 --> 00:55:46,343
They don’t care about us,
annie.

1282
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:47,778
They just cut us loose.

1283
00:55:47,778 --> 00:55:50,948
In fact,
everybody cut footloose.

1284
00:55:50,948 --> 00:55:55,187
Is terry jo’s brother
still running with
the 12th street gang?

1285
00:55:55,187 --> 00:55:57,122
Yeah.

1286
00:55:57,122 --> 00:55:59,123
Can you set up
a meeting with me?

1287
00:55:59,123 --> 00:56:00,125
What for?

1288
00:56:00,125 --> 00:56:02,127
You’re such a nun.

1289
00:56:02,127 --> 00:56:03,862
So he can shoot me.

1290
00:56:03,862 --> 00:56:04,862
[Laughs]

1291
00:56:04,862 --> 00:56:06,330
We’re sharing
a vague moment.

1292
00:56:06,330 --> 00:56:07,265
[Laughs]

1293
00:56:09,033 --> 00:56:10,835
Ladies and gentlemen,

1294
00:56:10,835 --> 00:56:11,903
fred burroughs.

1295
00:56:11,903 --> 00:56:13,838
[Laughter]

1296
00:56:16,673 --> 00:56:19,910
We’re number one.

1297
00:56:19,910 --> 00:56:22,580
Based on a play by
terrence mcnally.

1298
00:56:29,287 --> 00:56:31,088
Hmm?

1299
00:56:31,088 --> 00:56:32,957
Maybe he is
tom of finland.

1300
00:56:32,957 --> 00:56:34,892
Could be.

1301
00:56:38,195 --> 00:56:39,563
Hey, little pal.

1302
00:56:39,563 --> 00:56:41,498
Where’d my thumb go?

1303
00:56:43,768 --> 00:56:45,035
Cha.

1304
00:56:45,035 --> 00:56:46,037
Cha.

1305
00:56:46,037 --> 00:56:47,372
Cha.

1306
